                "note": "\"rounded off to the nearest multiple of 10 ignoring any part of a rupee consisting of paise and thereafter if such amount is not a multiple of ten\" -- increased if the last figure is five or more, reduced if it is less than five. Dropping the paise first and rounding the whole-rupee figure on its last digit gives the same answer as rounding the exact amount half upward, because the paise can only decide the outcome at an exact rupee ending in five, where both readings round up."
